----- 旧 0099：BACKPORT: UPSTREAM: rcu: Track laziness during boot and suspend -----
Author: Joel Fernandes (Google) <joel@joelfernandes.org>

Boot and suspend/resume should not be slowed down in kernels built with CONFIG_RCU_LAZY=y. Add rcu_async_hurry(), rcu_async_relax(), and rcu_async_should_hurry() to track whether boot or suspend/resume is in progress.

Backported from ACK android14-5.15 commit 856859371956b4d39ad7affe286f516d8253e736.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

----- 旧 0100：BACKPORT: FROMLIST: rcu: Provide a boot time parameter to control lazy RCU -----
Author: Qais Yousef <qyousef@layalina.io>

Add rcutree.enable_rcu_lazy (writable at runtime), default off via CONFIG_RCU_LAZY_DEFAULT_OFF. Also honor rcu_async_should_hurry() so boot and suspend never use lazy callbacks, and rename call_rcu_flush() to call_rcu_hurry() to match upstream.

Backported from ACK android14-5.15 commits 856859371956, 706e751b3331 and 37b02c190cbf.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

----- 旧 0101：BACKPORT: workqueue: Make queue_rcu_work() use call_rcu_hurry() -----
Author: Uladzislau Rezki <urezki@gmail.com>

queue_rcu_work() callers are not necessarily OK with long delays, and dst_release() is on the network fast path. Use call_rcu_hurry() for both.

Backported from ACK android14-5.15 commit a7e30c0e9a5f and upstream dst_release change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

----- 旧 0102：BACKPORT: rcu/nocb: Fix lazy shrinker races and offload handling -----
Author: Frederic Weisbecker <frederic@kernel.org>

Backport the 5.15 fixes that make the lazy-callback shrinker iterate only over NOCB CPUs, recheck lazy_len under ->nocb_lock, flush the bypass list through rcu_nocb_flush_bypass(), and protect against concurrent (de-)offloading with barrier_mutex.

Backported from ACK android14-5.15 commits 2450b78e0bb1, fbde57d2d299, b96a8b0b5be4, 762592608676 and 5c83cedbaaad, adapted from tree_nocb.h to 5.10 tree_plugin.h.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

----- 旧 0103：scsi: use call_rcu_hurry() for EH host_failed update -----
Author: OneFeiFan <3022504358@qq.com>

scsi_eh_scmd_add() queues scsi_eh_inc_host_failed via call_rcu() to order the host state change before host_failed. With RCU lazy callbacks enabled, that callback could be delayed up to 10 seconds, delaying the SCSI/UFS error handler and recovery. Use call_rcu_hurry() to keep the existing bounded-time behavior.

Found by the r14 call_rcu audit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
